      <article class="worship-letter ways-letter">
        <div class="worship-celestial" aria-hidden="true"><span class="worship-moon">☾</span><span class="worship-star worship-star-one">✦</span><span class="worship-star worship-star-two">✧</span><span class="worship-cloud worship-cloud-one"></span><span class="worship-cloud worship-cloud-two"></span></div>
        <header class="worship-intro ways-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A note from your goddess</p><p class="worship-constellation" aria-hidden="true">✦&nbsp;✧&nbsp;✦</p><h1>Ways to <em>Worship.</em></h1></header>
        <div class="worship-prose ways-prose">
          <p>The moon never begs for attention. She just pulls the tide, and everything obeys. I've always thought she and I had a lot in common.</p>
          <p>The ones who stand out are never forgotten. They're the ones I remember.</p>
          <p>Now. Pay attention, because I'm only writing this once.</p>
          <p>I am La Davina Emilia. I am a goddess, and I live like one, because I built this life and I keep it. I already have money. I don't need yours. I want it, and more than that, I want what your tribute means: that you looked at my life, my standards, my world, and decided it deserved a piece of yours.</p>
          <p>I am not a cruel goddess. I don't scream, I don't insult, and I don't traffic in humiliation for the masses. My punishment is far more effective: I go quiet, and I tell you I'm disappointed. If you know, you know. If you don't yet, you will.</p>
          <p>My rules are three, and they are simple, and they are not negotiable. Read them. Learn them. Then start at the beginning, the way everyone does.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="/rules.php">Read the Rules <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
          <hr class="ways-divider">
          <p class="eyebrow">An offering, properly made</p>
          <p>Money is how you say it. This is how you send it.</p>
          <p>Every avenue below reaches me. Choose the one that fits the moment, and know that how you tribute tells me as much as how much.</p>
          <section class="ways-list" aria-label="Tribute avenues">
            <article class="way-card"><p class="eyebrow">Throne <em>(the classic)</em></p><p>My wishlist and my gift throne. The everyday avenue for the devoted. Small tributes, wishlist pieces, spontaneous offerings. If you're new and nervous, start here. It's the gentlest way to make yourself known to me.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="https://throne.com/ladavinaemilia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit my Throne <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="way-card"><p class="eyebrow">Direct Tribute <em>(the statement)</em></p><p>YouPay, for the devoted one who wants their tribute to arrive directly, discreetly, and without ceremony. Neutral on your statements. Unmistakable in its meaning. This is for tributes with intent.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="https://youpay.me/ladavinaemilia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Offer a direct tribute <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
            <article class="way-card"><p class="eyebrow">Crypto <em>(the private)</em></p><p>For my privacy-minded ones and my big sends. No chargebacks, no questions, no trail. Ask me properly and I'll provide my wallet. If you don't know how to use it, that's a you problem, and I say that with love.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:hi@ladavinaemilia.com?subject=Crypto%20wallet%20request">Contact for my wallet <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
          </section>
          <hr class="ways-divider">
          <section class="first-tributes" aria-labelledby="first-tributes-title">
            <p class="eyebrow">Your first offering</p>
            <h2 id="first-tributes-title">Your First <em>Tribute.</em></h2>
            <p>The scariest send is the first one. I know. I've watched hundreds of people make it, and I've never once watched one regret it.</p>
            <p>So let's remove every ounce of mystery from it, because nerves come from not knowing, and knowing is free.</p>
            <h3>What a first tribute <em>actually is.</em></h3>
            <p>Your first tribute is not a purchase. It's not a payment, and it's not a fee. It's an introduction, the first full sentence you'll ever say to me in the only language that never lies.</p>
            <p>Everything before it—the reading, the Rules, the intake—is you telling me you're serious. The first tribute is you showing me. It's the moment you stop being a visitor and become a Sub under consideration, and yes, I remember every first tribute. I remember the amount, the avenue, and usually the hour it arrived. Firsts matter. I treat them that way.</p>
            <h3>How much should you <em>send?</em></h3>
            <p>However much is honest.</p>
            <p>I don't set first-tribute minimums, and I never will, because a number I assign tells me nothing about you. A number you choose tells me everything. Your first tribute is you answering one question, in your own hand: “What is she worth to me, right now, today, honestly?” Send the answer to that question and you literally never get it wrong.</p>
            <p>Two pieces of guidance, offered gently:</p>
            <ul class="first-tribute-notes"><li><strong>Don't send big to impress.</strong> The Sub who sends their rent money in week one isn't devoted; they're reckless, and I don't keep reckless Subs, I worry about them. Impress me with your judgment first. There will be time for grand gestures once I know you're well.</li><li><strong>Don't send small to test.</strong> A tribute so tiny it's really just a knock on the door is not a first tribute; it's a question, and it gets treated like one. If what you actually want is to look around more, look around more. My site is free. My attention isn't.</li></ul>
            <h3>Which avenue to <em>use.</em></h3>
            <p>If you're new and your hands are shaking a little, use <a href="https://throne.com/ladavinaemilia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Throne</a>. It's the gentlest way in: wishlist pieces, small offerings, no ceremony required. It exists precisely for firsts.</p>
            <p>If you already know this is who you are and what you want, <a href="https://youpay.me/ladavinaemilia" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YouPay</a> sends your tribute directly, discreetly, with nothing on your statement that raises an eyebrow at the bank or at a kitchen table.</p>
            <p>Crypto is for the privacy-minded and the substantial sends. Ask me properly and I'll provide my wallet.</p>
            <p>Every avenue is listed above, with a line about when each one belongs in your hands.</p>
            <h3>The etiquette, in <em>four lines.</em></h3>
            <ul class="first-tribute-notes"><li>Send it with your name or intake reference, so I know it's yours. An anonymous tribute is a gift with no giver, and I don't know what to do with those.</li><li>Don't announce it like a favor. “I sent you something, Goddess” lands very differently than “I demanded you notice my generosity.” One of those gets a warm reply. Guess which.</li><li>Don't ask what it buys you. It doesn't buy anything. It says something. What it says is up to you.</li><li>Then let it breathe. I acknowledge tributes when I see them, in my own time, in my own way. The waiting is part of it. The waiting is the first thing I'll ever teach you.</li></ul>
            <h3>And for the nervous ones, one last <em>thing.</em></h3>
            <p>Your first tribute doesn't have to be big. It doesn't have to be brave. It only has to be yours.</p>
            <p>Send what feels honest, send it with your name on it, and know that I remember the ones who start. Every kept Sub I've ever had started exactly here, exactly this nervous, exactly this unsure.</p>
            <p class="ways-closing">The ones who made it weren't the ones who sent the most.</p>
            <p class="ways-closing">They were the ones who sent first. 💋</p>
          </section>
          <p>A note on gifts: I appreciate my money above all things. If you're going to send a gift instead, understand that it must be extraordinary to compete with cash. My Throne wishlist exists because I've already curated it. Anything outside it had better be exceptional, or expensive, and ideally both.</p>
          <p>And a note for the record: tributes are just that, tributes. Gifts freely given to a goddess. I don't refund them, and I don't negotiate with them. A Sub who tributes me has made a decision, and I respect their decisions, which is more than I can say for most people in their life.</p>
          <p class="ways-closing">Choose your avenue. Make your offering.</p>
          <p class="ways-signoff">The moon is always pulling. 💋</p>
